==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*stōdą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*sta-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*stə-||stand, set}}. Cognate with Old High German {{m|goh|stuot||herd of horses}} (German {{m|de|Stute||mare}}), Old Norse {{m|non|stóð}} (Swedish {{m|sv|sto||mare}}). The Indo-European root is also the source of Albanian {{m|sq|shtazë||animal, beast}} and Old Slavic ''stado''<!--wrong script for Old Slavic-->

